# FuckClaude Project Conventions

## Tech Stack & Architecture
- **Framework**: Astro (SSG/SSR hybrid via `@astrojs/vercel`) + TypeScript.
- **Production Domain**: `https://fuck-claude.vercel.app` (canonical). Custom domains (`fuckclaude.tech`, `www.fuckclaude.tech`) 308 redirect to this origin.
- **Styling**: Scoped CSS using site-wide CSS variables (`var(--surface)`, `var(--border)`, `var(--accent)`, `var(--mono)`, etc.).
- **Mobile header**: The shared `.nav` / `.nav__actions` / `.brand__text` styles live in `src/layouts/BaseLayout.astro`. At `max-width: 560px` the brand collapses to the logo and `.nav__actions` wraps onto a second row. New header items must not break this; verify `documentElement.scrollWidth === viewport width` at 320/360/375/414px on `/`, `/zh/`, `/guides/`, `/news/`, and spot-check RTL locales such as `/ar/` and long-word locales such as `/my/`.
- **Grids and long tokens**: Use `minmax(min(Npx, 100%), 1fr)` for `auto-fill` grids, and `overflow-wrap: anywhere` on cards that render user-facing text with long identifiers (env vars, model names).

## Locales & i18n
- **Registry**: `src/i18n/locales.ts` exports `LOCALES`, `Lang`, `localePath`, `stripLocalePrefix`, `alternatePaths`, and helpers. English is at `/`; other locales use a path prefix (`/zh/`, `/ru/`, `/fa/`, `/es/`, `/ar/`, `/my/`). Do not hardcode locale unions or `lang === 'zh'` toggles; use the registry and `localize` / `useTranslations`.
- **Config copy**: `{ en, zh }` objects in `src/config/*` and trust content resolve through `localize(record, lang)` (`src/i18n/localize.ts`). Order: native `en`/`zh`, dictionary (`src/i18n/translations/<lang>/*.ts`, keys = exact English source), then English fallback.
- **UI strings**: Keys live in `src/i18n/ui.ts` (`en` + `zh` bases). Overlays per locale: `src/i18n/messages/<lang>.ts` (partial key map). Client code uses `src/i18n/ui-client.ts` and reads `data-lang` on `<html>`.
- **Guide bodies**: Default HTML in `src/content/guides/*.ts` + `guidesData.ts`. Per-locale overrides: `src/content/guides-i18n/<lang>/<slug>.ts` exporting `content: string`. Resolution in `src/i18n/guide-content.ts` (override → English).
- **Routes**: Prefixed locales use `src/pages/[lang]/*` with `getStaticPaths` over `PREFIXED_LOCALES`. English stays under `src/pages/*` without a prefix. Shared page shells take a `lang` prop (`Detector`, `GuidesHubPage`, `GuideArticlePage`, `NewsHubPage`, etc.).
- **SEO**: Breadcrumbs, `hreflang`, `og:locale`, and JSON-LD `inLanguage` must list every locale plus `x-default` → English. No automatic redirects from `Accept-Language` (suggestion banner only: `LocaleSuggestBanner.astro`). Guide pages that fall back to the English body set `noindex` and omit that locale from `hreflang`.
- **Locale data store**: Dictionaries and message overlays are registered in `src/i18n/locale-data.ts`. The server fills it eagerly (`locale-data-server.ts`, imported by `localize.ts` and `use-translations.ts`). The browser fills it per locale (`locale-data-client.ts`); client scripts call `await loadLocaleData(langFromDocument())` before `useTranslations`. Never import every locale eagerly in client code. Wrap `import.meta.glob` in try/catch (`typeof import.meta.glob` is false at build time). Adding a locale needs no aggregator edit: add the registry row and the files.
- **Dynamic strings**: Server messages that reach users (`src/i18n/api-messages.ts`, `HINT`/`NOTICE` in `src/server/ip-purity.ts`, `CHECK_JSON_NOTE`) are `Localized` records or dictionary keys. Raw detection values in `src/config/signals.ts` and `src/pages/api/check.ts` (for example `none detected`) are still English-only in every locale.
- **Machine translation**: Non-native locales (`ru`, `fa`, `es`, `ar`, `my`) show `I18nNotice.astro`. Texts have no native-speaker review. When the English source changes, the dictionary key changes and the entry falls back to English until retranslated.
- **Country framing**: In `ru`, `fa`, `es`, `ar`, `my`, labels and explanatory prose (page title, hero, badges, result bands, share text, `how.*`, `why.*`, `reduce.*`, `faq.*`, privacy/IP texts, API check label) name the locale's country (Россия, ایران, Cuba, سوريا, မြန်မာ), and signal names use neutral wording ("regional", "local"). The detector still checks only China signals. Keep the literal identifiers it checks (`Asia/Shanghai`, `Asia/Urumqi`, `zh-CN`, `UTC+8`, brand and font names) and do not invent per-country time zones, language tags, or device brands. Statements that Anthropic does not offer Claude in the country must stay true against `https://www.anthropic.com/supported-countries`. Statements that Claude Code treats that country's traffic as higher risk have no source; they exist because the product owner asked for the country framing. `cnModels.*` and policy or news facts about China stay unchanged.
- **RTL**: `fa` and `ar` set `<html dir="rtl">`. Use logical CSS properties (`inset-inline-*`, `margin-inline-*`, `text-align: start`) in new styles, not `left`/`right`.
- **Coverage and validation**: `npm run i18n:coverage` reports missing UI overlays, dictionary entries, and guide bodies (`--export=<lang>` writes `/tmp/i18n-<lang>-missing.json`). `npm run i18n:validate -- <ru|fa|es|ar|my>` checks key sets, placeholders, and guide HTML structure against English; run it after editing any translation file.

## News & Community Content
- **News**: Maintained in `src/config/news.ts`. Items use `{ en, zh }` fields (title, summary, takeaway, etc.) plus category tag and source link. `publishedAt` must match the date on the cited source page (for example the Transparency Hub's "Last updated" date), not the date the item was added.
- **Non-official news items** (media or community reports, such as regional ban waves): cite the original publisher in `sourceName`, cross-check at least two independent sources, and state that Anthropic has not confirmed causes or scale. Do not cite vendor blogs that sell a competing service as the sole source.
- **Social / X Community Posts**: Maintained in `src/config/community-posts.ts` and rendered via `src/components/CommunityPosts.astro`. Must retain direct links to original X posts, author name, handle, profile link, tags, and practical takeaways. Verify each post before adding it (author, date, text) through `https://api.fxtwitter.com/<handle>/status/<id>`. Never add posts that cannot be verified, and do not repeat advice that tells users to open replacement accounts after a ban. Available tags are defined in `POST_TAGS`; each tag also needs a `data-tag` colour rule in `CommunityPosts.astro`.
- **News filtering**: `ClaudeNews.astro` and `getLatestNews()` accept `categories`; the guides hub shows only `policy` and `security` items, after the guide catalog.
- **Community post links**: Every post in `community-posts.ts` sets `relatedGuideSlug`; `CommunityPosts.astro` renders it as a "Related guide" link.

## Guides
- **Single source of truth**: `src/config/guides.ts` holds all guide metadata (slug, category, `{ en, zh }` title/summary, `publishedAt`, `updatedAt`, optional `verifiedAt`, curated `related`, `sources`, `listed`). `updatedAt` exists only there. Bodies live in `src/content/guides/*.ts` and are registered in `src/content/guidesData.ts` as `GUIDE_CONTENT`. Adding a guide means touching those three places.
- **Pages**: `/guides/`, `/zh/guides/`, `/ru/guides/`, … share `GuidesHubPage.astro` and `GuideArticlePage.astro` (both take `lang`). The hub catalog is `GuideCatalog.astro`; the official-rules block is `OfficialRules.astro`. Do not copy these pages per language.
- **Official facts**: Statements about Anthropic policy (supported regions, ban reasons, appeals, accepted payment methods, rate limits, transparency numbers) must link to an official page through `OFFICIAL_SOURCES` in `guides.ts`. `src/config/official-rules.ts` feeds the hub block; re-check it and bump `OFFICIAL_RULES_CHECKED_AT` and the guide's `verifiedAt` whenever one of those facts changes. Region facts must also match `https://www.anthropic.com/supported-countries` and `src/config/signals.ts`.
- **No unsourced numbers**: Do not publish card BINs, "success rate" or "pass rate" figures, or savings percentages without a source. Label community observations as such. Do not recommend specific card types or BINs as "safe", and do not promise that any setup avoids bans.
- **Hidden guides**: `listed: false` keeps a guide reachable by URL but removes it from the hub, home page, and related lists (`claude-ai-content-watermarking`).
- **Article HTML**: Bodies are HTML strings. `prepareArticleHtml()` in `src/utils/guide-html.ts` adds heading ids, builds the table of contents, and wraps every `<table>` in `.table-scroll`; do not add your own table wrappers. Dates use `YYYY-MM-DD` (`YYYY-MM` is padded to the first of the month for JSON-LD).
- **Chinese punctuation**: Chinese text uses full-width punctuation (，。？！；：). Keep ASCII punctuation inside code, identifiers, and English phrases.

## Sponsors
- **Sponsors Config**: Maintained in `src/config/sponsors.ts` and rendered via `src/components/Sponsors.astro`. Logos live under `public/sponsors/`. Entries include `{ en, zh }` headlines, taglines, CTAs, and referral URLs. Sponsor copy describes the product neutrally and must not promise to bypass Claude risk control or avoid bans.

## Detection Signals
- Fingerprint detection signals live in `src/config/signals.ts` with sum of weights = 100.
- Detection must run client-side only without uploading user data. Follow `skills/detection-signals/SKILL.md`.
